1
00:00:03,900 --> 00:00:05,440
Thank you guys for having us over.

2
00:00:06,180 --> 00:00:07,880
Yeah, this is fun, couples night.

3
00:00:08,460 --> 00:00:09,560
I don't know why we don't hang out...

4
00:00:09,560 --> 00:00:10,700
...with married couples more often.

5
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:12,460
Because every time we do...

6
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:14,180
...you make jokes about swinging

7
00:00:14,180 --> 00:00:15,120
and scare them away.

8
00:00:17,260 --> 00:00:18,660
You mean that Portuguese couple?

9
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:20,660
Yeah, like you wouldn't have done it.

10
00:00:23,360 --> 00:00:25,780
Hey, you guys, I have great news.

11
00:00:26,600 --> 00:00:27,420
We're kind of in the middle of dinner.

12
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:30,620
Oh, well, I already ate, but sure.

13
00:00:33,120 --> 00:00:34,560
Guess what happened at work today.

14
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:36,560
A dinosaur died a million years ago?

15
00:00:37,960 --> 00:00:40,780
Try 65 million years ago. And then try...

16
00:00:43,760 --> 00:00:45,420
My tenure review board met today,

17
00:00:45,420 --> 00:00:47,580
and I hear it's looking really good.

18
00:00:48,680 --> 00:00:49,800
Yeah, do you have any idea

19
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,420
what this means in academic circles?

20
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:53,480
I am gonna get laid.

21
00:00:56,580 --> 00:00:58,040
- Hi, you guys. - Hey.

22
00:00:58,040 --> 00:00:58,980
Oh, ltalian.

23
00:01:00,540 --> 00:01:02,480
No one-- No one wanted seconds, right?

24
00:01:02,560 --> 00:01:03,560
No, I'm good.

25
00:01:05,380 --> 00:01:06,400
Guys, you're never gonna believe it.

26
00:01:06,400 --> 00:01:07,760
This headhunter called me.

27
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:10,160
Gucci:著名意大利奢侈品品牌

28
00:01:08,000 --> 00:01:09,500
I have a meeting tomorrow with Gucci.

29
00:01:10,040 --> 00:01:11,780
Gucci wants me.

30
00:01:11,980 --> 00:01:14,200
- I'm up for tenure. - Congratulations.

31
00:01:14,220 --> 00:01:15,640
You too. What are the odds?

32
00:01:17,280 --> 00:01:17,920
Guess what?

33
00:01:19,660 --> 00:01:21,560
I finally got that seed out of my teeth.

34
00:01:24,760 --> 00:01:25,980
I don't know who I'm happiest for.

35
00:01:26,000 --> 00:01:29,300
I do. He's been working on that all day.

36
00:01:30,827 --> 00:01:32,827
《老友记》第十季第十四集 "康斯薇拉公主"驾到

37
00:02:22,260 --> 00:02:23,460
Hey, Mon, was it weird

38
00:02:23,460 --> 00:02:24,860
changing your name to Geller Bing?

39
00:02:25,620 --> 00:02:28,660
No. No, it felt nice to acknowledge this.

40
00:02:29,320 --> 00:02:30,680
- Where'd you go to do it? - The--

41
00:02:33,000 --> 00:02:34,360
The Ministry of Names...

42
00:02:36,820 --> 00:02:37,700
...Bureau.

43
00:02:38,880 --> 00:02:40,160
You never did it.

44
00:02:40,200 --> 00:02:42,920
I'm sorry. It's just the idea of--

45
00:02:42,940 --> 00:02:44,760
Of being an official Bing.

46
00:02:47,340 --> 00:02:49,500
Hey, I will have you know that--

47
00:02:50,460 --> 00:02:52,080
Who am I kidding? Let's call the kid Geller

48
00:02:52,080 --> 00:02:53,460
and let Bing die with me.

49
00:02:55,859 --> 00:02:56,879
- Here you go. - Thanks.

50
00:02:57,140 --> 00:02:59,020
Honey, would you want me to take your name?

51
00:02:59,900 --> 00:03:01,120
Oh, it's up to you.

52
00:03:01,280 --> 00:03:01,620
It's your name.

53
00:03:01,640 --> 00:03:02,680
You've gotta live with it.

54
00:03:03,340 --> 00:03:04,840
Let's see. Call me Mrs. Hannigan.

55
00:03:05,140 --> 00:03:05,880
Mrs. Hannigan?

56
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,860
What? Can't you see I'm in the middle of something?

57
00:03:10,240 --> 00:03:11,040
I like it.

58
00:03:12,760 --> 00:03:14,380
- Hey, guys. - Hey, Joe.

59
00:03:14,500 --> 00:03:15,160
We've got a couple of things

60
00:03:15,180 --> 00:03:16,620
we've got to check out at the new house.

61
00:03:16,680 --> 00:03:17,680
You want to come?

62
00:03:17,700 --> 00:03:18,940
No, thank you.

63
00:03:20,240 --> 00:03:21,440
You're not happy about us moving...

64
00:03:21,440 --> 00:03:23,180
...but you're the only one who hasn't seen the house.

65
00:03:23,180 --> 00:03:24,060
Yeah, come with us.

66
00:03:24,060 --> 00:03:25,020
You'll see how close it is.

67
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:27,200
No, it's not close.

68
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:29,180
in escrow:根据协议由第三方保管  乔伊以为是地名

69
00:03:27,720 --> 00:03:28,760
You said it was in escrow.

70
00:03:29,080 --> 00:03:30,480
I couldn't even find that on the map.

71
00:03:34,642 --> 00:03:36,240
Joey, please come.

72
00:03:36,260 --> 00:03:37,560
It would mean so much to us.

73
00:03:40,160 --> 00:03:40,900
You know what?

74
00:03:41,240 --> 00:03:42,080
You are my friends.

75
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:43,260
I want to be supportive.

76
00:03:43,360 --> 00:03:44,620
I will come with you. Shotgun.

77
00:03:44,900 --> 00:03:45,340
Damn it.

78
00:03:46,400 --> 00:03:47,300
See you guys later.

79
00:03:47,640 --> 00:03:48,420
We'll pick you up at 11.

80
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:49,500
So glad you're coming.

81
00:03:49,605 --> 00:03:50,445
All right.

82
00:03:51,940 --> 00:03:52,920
Good for you.

83
00:03:52,940 --> 00:03:54,120
That was really mature.

84
00:03:54,180 --> 00:03:55,840
What? No, the only reason I'm going...

85
00:03:55,840 --> 00:03:57,520
...to their stupid house is

86
00:03:57,580 --> 00:03:59,280
to point out everything wrong with it...

87
00:03:59,280 --> 00:03:59,920
...so they don't move.

88
00:03:59,980 --> 00:04:01,000
I'm gonna make them stay here.

89
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,240
You're a strange kind of grownup.

90
00:04:06,240 --> 00:04:08,480
Joey, you can't make someone do something

91
00:04:08,480 --> 00:04:09,500
they don't want to do.

92
00:04:09,680 --> 00:04:10,220
Believe me.

93
00:04:10,320 --> 00:04:11,360
There's something I've been trying to

94
00:04:11,360 --> 00:04:12,760
get Mike to do in bed, and--

95
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:16,640
Can we not talk about that now?

96
00:04:16,700 --> 00:04:18,140
All right. Prude.

97
00:04:21,160 --> 00:04:22,820
Look, Monica and Chandler

98
00:04:22,820 --> 00:04:23,920
really love this house.

99
00:04:23,920 --> 00:04:25,820
You are not gonna talk them into staying here.

100
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,760
Hey, I can convince people to do anything, you know?

101
00:04:28,860 --> 00:04:30,640
I bet I could even get Mike to do that thing.

102
00:04:30,780 --> 00:04:31,480
What is it?

103
00:04:35,240 --> 00:04:37,520
I am not gonna help you do that!

104
00:04:38,380 --> 00:04:39,300
Oh, my God.

105
00:04:46,200 --> 00:04:50,000
Hi. I'm here to see Mr. Campbell, with Gucci.

106
00:04:50,920 --> 00:04:53,160
The reservation's probably under Gucci.

107
00:04:53,820 --> 00:04:55,140
It's spelled like "Gukki"

108
00:04:55,300 --> 00:04:56,280
which can be confusing.

109
00:04:58,180 --> 00:04:59,400
Mr.Campbell's not here yet.

110
00:04:59,420 --> 00:05:00,760
Let me show you to his table.

111
00:05:05,100 --> 00:05:07,120
Oh, my God. That's my boss.

112
00:05:07,240 --> 00:05:08,360
You have to seat us somewhere else.

113
00:05:08,700 --> 00:05:09,180
I'm sorry,

114
00:05:09,220 --> 00:05:11,020
that's always Mr.Campbell's table.

115
00:05:11,240 --> 00:05:13,020
But my boss cannot see me.

116
00:05:13,020 --> 00:05:15,020
I'm interviewing for another job.

117
00:05:15,200 --> 00:05:16,760
I know. With "Gukki."

118
00:05:19,900 --> 00:05:22,860
- Rachel? - I'm on a date.

119
00:05:24,780 --> 00:05:25,820
That's great.

120
00:05:26,460 --> 00:05:27,660
Yeah, it is.

121
00:05:27,890 --> 00:05:29,200
Yeah, you know, it's tough.

122
00:05:29,340 --> 00:05:30,340
Single mom. Career.

123
00:05:30,480 --> 00:05:31,760
You gotta get out there.

124
00:05:33,460 --> 00:05:35,480
Well, you've got a good energy.

125
00:05:37,040 --> 00:05:38,240
- Rachel? - Yes, hi.

126
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:39,540
- James Campbell. - Hi.

127
00:05:40,140 --> 00:05:41,380
- Excuse us. - Please.

128
00:05:45,080 --> 00:05:46,560
He's cute.

129
00:05:47,780 --> 00:05:48,780
So...

130
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:51,860
...your resume is quite impressive.

131
00:05:54,583 --> 00:05:56,103
My resume?

132
00:05:56,360 --> 00:05:57,840
I wouldn't-- I wouldn't call

133
00:05:57,840 --> 00:06:00,820
my online dating profile a resume.

134
00:06:02,100 --> 00:06:03,060
Dating profile?

135
00:06:03,120 --> 00:06:05,160
No, I'm-- I'm talking about the work resume.

136
00:06:09,100 --> 00:06:10,140
Whatever happened to

137
00:06:10,140 --> 00:06:11,900
just singing for no reason?

138
00:06:13,740 --> 00:06:15,680
Maybe people found it weird.

139
00:06:18,464 --> 00:06:19,504
So....

140
00:06:21,080 --> 00:06:22,320
Why do you want to leave Ralph Lauren?

141
00:06:22,640 --> 00:06:23,180
What?

142
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:25,660
- I...I don't. - You don't?

143
00:06:25,680 --> 00:06:27,000
No, I love-- I love it there.

144
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,340
Well, if you don't want to leave,

145
00:06:28,340 --> 00:06:29,540
why are we having this lunch?

146
00:06:33,760 --> 00:06:34,200
What?

147
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,700
Hugo Boss:德国奢侈品品牌

148
00:06:37,360 --> 00:06:38,440
That's Hugo Boss?

149
00:06:45,600 --> 00:06:47,680
This place is so depressing.

150
00:06:48,060 --> 00:06:48,880
If I had to work here,

151
00:06:48,900 --> 00:06:49,720
I'd kill myself.

152
00:06:53,220 --> 00:06:54,920
But you obviously haven't.

153
00:06:57,300 --> 00:06:58,180
How can I help you?

154
00:06:58,180 --> 00:07:00,060
I need to change my name, please.

155
00:07:00,400 --> 00:07:02,920
See, I need to change it because I'm hiding from the law.

156
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:07,000
You're fun.

157
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,720
You need to fill out this form.

158
00:07:09,820 --> 00:07:10,680
Okay. Well, just so I know--

159
00:07:10,700 --> 00:07:13,820
I don't know how it works. My name is Buffay...

160
00:07:13,990 --> 00:07:15,380
...and my husband's name is Hannigan.

161
00:07:15,800 --> 00:07:17,520
So is it supposed to be "Buffay-Hannigan"

162
00:07:17,520 --> 00:07:18,360
or "Hannigan-Buffay"?

163
00:07:18,780 --> 00:07:20,200
It can be anything you want.

164
00:07:20,540 --> 00:07:21,460
Well, not anything.

165
00:07:21,801 --> 00:07:23,771
Yeah. Anything.

166
00:07:25,400 --> 00:07:26,940
Oh, this could take a while.

167
00:07:29,340 --> 00:07:30,620
- Get out of my line. - Okay.

168
00:07:36,440 --> 00:07:37,940
- Hey. - Hey, Pheebs.

169
00:07:38,180 --> 00:07:40,440
Oh, not anymore. I changed it today.

170
00:07:40,560 --> 00:07:42,520
Oh, I'm sorry, Mrs. Hannigan.

171
00:07:42,740 --> 00:07:43,520
Wrong again.

172
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:48,080
Apparently, you can change it to anything.

173
00:07:48,600 --> 00:07:49,440
So I thought, "All right,

174
00:07:49,440 --> 00:07:51,160
here's an opportunity to be creative."

175
00:07:51,500 --> 00:07:55,100
So meet Princess Consuela Banana Hammock.

176
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:03,900
That's what we were gonna name the baby.

177
00:08:07,126 --> 00:08:09,906
- Phoebe. - Princess Consuela.

178
00:08:11,140 --> 00:08:13,200
You seriously changed your name to that?

179
00:08:13,780 --> 00:08:14,660
Okay, so from now on,

180
00:08:14,660 --> 00:08:16,420
we have to call you Princess Consuela?

181
00:08:17,080 --> 00:08:19,080
No, I'm gonna have my friends call me Valerie.

182
00:08:24,020 --> 00:08:27,340
- Hey, how did the interview go? - Not good.

183
00:08:27,720 --> 00:08:29,780
You know. I always feel that way after an interview.

184
00:08:29,840 --> 00:08:31,160
I'll bet it went better than you think.

185
00:08:32,160 --> 00:08:34,120
Well, I didn't get the job at Gucci

186
00:08:34,280 --> 00:08:36,240
and I got fired from Ralph Lauren.

187
00:08:37,000 --> 00:08:38,040
That is a bad interview.

188
00:08:39,740 --> 00:08:40,940
What are you talking about?

189
00:08:40,960 --> 00:08:42,080
How did this happen?

190
00:08:42,320 --> 00:08:44,900
My boss was at the same restaurant

191
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:46,320
where I was having my interview...

192
00:08:46,350 --> 00:08:47,400
...and he heard everything.

193
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,560
Later, he calls me into his office

194
00:08:49,560 --> 00:08:51,740
and tells me he'll have to let me go...

195
00:08:52,040 --> 00:08:53,340
...because I'm not a team player.

196
00:08:53,340 --> 00:08:55,420
And I said, "Wait a minute. Yes, I am."

197
00:08:55,420 --> 00:08:58,360
And then I had to sit there for 45 minutes...

198
00:08:58,360 --> 00:09:02,480
...while he proved that that, in fact, was true.

199
00:09:04,340 --> 00:09:05,760
Oh, God, I'm so sorry.

200
00:09:07,700 --> 00:09:08,280
Hey.

201
00:09:09,300 --> 00:09:11,400
What--? What's this?

202
00:09:12,420 --> 00:09:14,540
Why, it's a bottle of champagne.

203
00:09:15,020 --> 00:09:16,260
Why is this here?

204
00:09:16,360 --> 00:09:17,840
- Ross. - I guess it's here...

205
00:09:17,840 --> 00:09:19,680
...because I got tenure!

206
00:09:20,140 --> 00:09:21,060
- Congratulations. - Congratulations.

207
00:09:21,760 --> 00:09:25,100
This is the single greatest day of my professional career.

208
00:09:25,560 --> 00:09:27,760
- Gunther. Six glasses. - Six?

209
00:09:27,900 --> 00:09:29,140
You want me to join you?

210
00:09:29,500 --> 00:09:30,320
I thought Joey was here.

211
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:30,960
Five is good.

212
00:09:35,060 --> 00:09:37,180
Wow, I'm gonna have a loogey in my coffee tomorrow.

213
00:09:39,518 --> 00:09:41,458
Israeli champagne.

214
00:09:42,220 --> 00:09:43,020
And it's vanilla.

215
00:09:44,700 --> 00:09:46,720
I got tenure. I didn't win the lottery.

216
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:50,680
Hey, Rach, so how did your thing go?

217
00:09:50,897 --> 00:09:51,927
Good.

218
00:09:52,100 --> 00:09:54,220
But I'm not going to hear about that for a couple days.

219
00:09:54,220 --> 00:09:55,720
Oh, you know what, you're gonna get it.

220
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:57,320
I can feel it.

221
00:09:57,320 --> 00:09:57,940
Can you?

222
00:09:59,760 --> 00:10:01,360
All right, everybody, here's to Ross.

223
00:10:01,661 --> 00:10:06,480
And to years of hard work finally paying off.

224
00:10:06,500 --> 00:10:09,300
And to knowing that your career

225
00:10:09,300 --> 00:10:10,460
doesn't mean everything.

226
00:10:10,700 --> 00:10:13,560
But also knowing it means a lot.

227
00:10:15,500 --> 00:10:18,140
But more importantly, to full, well-rounded lives.

228
00:10:18,160 --> 00:10:19,560
That center around work.

229
00:10:20,046 --> 00:10:22,126
- To Ross. - To Ross.

230
00:10:26,240 --> 00:10:28,200
You know what the best part about this is?

231
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:29,560
I can never be fired.

232
00:10:29,780 --> 00:10:31,160
- Oh, God. - No, seriously.

233
00:10:31,280 --> 00:10:33,800
I have job security for life.

234
00:10:34,210 --> 00:10:35,880
You know? I mean, I never have to worry.

235
00:10:36,500 --> 00:10:39,560
Oh, look at you. Look how happy you are for me.

236
00:10:42,400 --> 00:10:45,940
No, it's not that. I got fired today.

237
00:10:46,420 --> 00:10:47,920
And I didn't get the other job.

238
00:10:51,720 --> 00:10:53,120
Rach, I'm so sorry.

239
00:10:55,240 --> 00:10:56,480
Great, I feel like an idiot.

240
00:10:56,500 --> 00:10:57,900
No, it's okay. You didn't know.

241
00:11:00,500 --> 00:11:01,940
Little heads-up would've been nice.

242
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:13,540
Thank you for letting us see the house again.

243
00:11:13,560 --> 00:11:15,900
And thank you for explaining to us what escrow means.

244
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:17,800
I've already forgotten what you said,

245
00:11:17,880 --> 00:11:18,620
but thank you.

246
00:11:19,860 --> 00:11:21,000
Take as long as you want.

247
00:11:21,220 --> 00:11:22,200
Just let me know when you're through.

248
00:11:25,780 --> 00:11:27,000
So glad you decided to come.

249
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,800
Me too. Yeah, this place is great.

250
00:11:29,220 --> 00:11:30,540
So happy for you guys.

251
00:11:31,060 --> 00:11:32,520
Although, you know, I hope you like fungus.

252
00:11:35,340 --> 00:11:36,400
- What? - Fungus.

253
00:11:37,020 --> 00:11:38,260
Yeah. Place is full of it.

254
00:11:39,080 --> 00:11:40,060
No, it's not.

255
00:11:40,320 --> 00:11:41,200
We had an inspection

256
00:11:41,240 --> 00:11:42,220
and they didn't find anything.

257
00:11:42,280 --> 00:11:44,420
Okay. Then I guess I have dry eyes

258
00:11:44,420 --> 00:11:45,780
and a scratchy throat for no reason.

259
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,440
Maybe it's because you hung your head

260
00:11:47,440 --> 00:11:48,920
out the window like a dog...

261
00:11:48,920 --> 00:11:50,140
...the whole ride here.

262
00:11:52,860 --> 00:11:53,260
Maybe.

263
00:11:54,920 --> 00:11:56,480
So this is the living room, huh?

264
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:57,720
It's pretty dark.

265
00:12:02,540 --> 00:12:03,620
No, it's not.

266
00:12:03,640 --> 00:12:04,300
Are you kidding?

267
00:12:04,600 --> 00:12:06,400
I think I just saw a bat in the corner.

268
00:12:08,140 --> 00:12:09,700
When your head was hanging out the window,

269
00:12:09,760 --> 00:12:11,740
it didn't hit a mailbox, did it?

270
00:12:13,980 --> 00:12:14,380
Maybe.

271
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,900
Look, I just think you guys can do

272
00:12:17,900 --> 00:12:19,560
better than this house, you know?

273
00:12:19,800 --> 00:12:21,560
Or any other house for that matter.

274
00:12:21,700 --> 00:12:22,720
Oh, Joey.

275
00:12:23,720 --> 00:12:25,620
We know you're having a hard time with this, but we--

276
00:12:26,240 --> 00:12:26,740
We love it here.

277
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:28,600
Fine! Ok. If you love this house so much...

278
00:12:28,780 --> 00:12:30,140
...you should live here. Okay?

279
00:12:30,420 --> 00:12:32,120
I hope you get used to that weird humming sound.

280
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:37,180
- Joey, we know that's you. - No...

281
00:12:37,380 --> 00:12:38,320
...it's not.

282
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:47,200
- Welcome back. - I missed you.

283
00:12:47,340 --> 00:12:49,120
- Oh, me too. - So, what's new?

284
00:12:49,580 --> 00:12:51,660
Well, I am no longer Phoebe Buffay.

285
00:12:52,040 --> 00:12:53,400
That's great. You changed your name?

286
00:12:53,480 --> 00:12:54,320
Yes, I did.

287
00:12:55,260 --> 00:12:57,560
Meet Princess Consuela Banana Hammock.

288
00:13:00,200 --> 00:13:01,500
- You're kidding, right? - Nope.

289
00:13:02,800 --> 00:13:04,060
- You really did that? - Yep.

290
00:13:05,200 --> 00:13:06,540
You can't do that.

291
00:13:07,300 --> 00:13:07,820
Why?

292
00:13:08,620 --> 00:13:09,440
Why? It's fun.

293
00:13:09,580 --> 00:13:11,940
It's different. No one else has a name like it.

294
00:13:14,100 --> 00:13:15,180
Then I'm gonna change my name.

295
00:13:15,320 --> 00:13:17,760
Great. Okay, what are you gonna change it to?

296
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:18,920
Crap Bag.

297
00:13:21,460 --> 00:13:22,580
Mike Crap Bag?

298
00:13:22,720 --> 00:13:25,160
No. No "Mike." No, just "Crap Bag."

299
00:13:25,360 --> 00:13:27,060
First name: Crap. Last name: Bag.

300
00:13:28,780 --> 00:13:30,060
You're not serious, right?

301
00:13:30,100 --> 00:13:30,980
Yeah, I'm serious.

302
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:32,180
It's fun, it's different,

303
00:13:32,200 --> 00:13:33,620
and no one else has a name like that.

304
00:13:35,300 --> 00:13:36,560
Well, then great.

305
00:13:36,700 --> 00:13:38,560
If you love it, I love it.

306
00:13:38,560 --> 00:13:40,220
I do love it. And I love your name.

307
00:13:40,320 --> 00:13:41,620
I love Princess Consuela.

308
00:13:41,640 --> 00:13:42,860
And I love Crap.

309
00:13:53,480 --> 00:13:56,180
- Who are you? - Oh, hi. I'm Joey.

310
00:13:56,640 --> 00:13:58,660
My stupid friends are buying this house.

311
00:13:58,660 --> 00:13:59,240
Who are you?

312
00:13:59,460 --> 00:14:00,220
I'm Mackenzie.

313
00:14:01,380 --> 00:14:03,480
My stupid parents are selling this house.

314
00:14:05,340 --> 00:14:06,760
I hate my parents.

315
00:14:07,620 --> 00:14:09,020
I hate my friends.

316
00:14:12,880 --> 00:14:14,200
Look, there's gotta be a way

317
00:14:14,380 --> 00:14:15,800
that we can stop this from happening.

318
00:14:16,460 --> 00:14:17,040
Like what?

319
00:14:20,320 --> 00:14:23,420
Okay, you come with me and you tell them that the house is haunted.

320
00:14:23,700 --> 00:14:24,920
What are you, 8?

321
00:14:29,340 --> 00:14:31,140
Okay. Let's hear your great idea.

322
00:14:31,460 --> 00:14:32,780
I don't have any great ideas.

323
00:14:33,200 --> 00:14:33,940
I am 8.

324
00:14:37,900 --> 00:14:39,160
There's gotta be a way. I mean, you know...

325
00:14:39,540 --> 00:14:41,120
...if Monica and Chandler move here,

326
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,820
and Phoebe's married to Mike...

327
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:44,880
...that just leaves me and Ross and Rach.

328
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,680
You know what I mean?

329
00:14:47,200 --> 00:14:48,880
I really don't.

330
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:51,080
What am I gonna do?

331
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:52,980
I feel like I'm losing my friends.

332
00:14:53,500 --> 00:14:55,320
My parents say I'll make new friends.

333
00:14:55,760 --> 00:14:57,120
Yeah, sure, easy for you.

334
00:14:57,180 --> 00:14:58,900
You're young. Me? I'm set in my ways.

335
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:03,460
This is what my mom was talking about.

336
00:15:04,180 --> 00:15:05,260
Whiners are wieners.

337
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,400
Look, you want your friends to be happy, right?

338
00:15:13,460 --> 00:15:15,400
Yeah. Yeah, I guess. Yeah.

339
00:15:16,060 --> 00:15:17,760
Well, if moving here is gonna make them happy,

340
00:15:18,220 --> 00:15:19,420
don't you want them to do it?

341
00:15:20,779 --> 00:15:22,959
Yeah. Maybe.

342
00:15:24,400 --> 00:15:25,700
Then you've gotta let them go.

343
00:15:31,420 --> 00:15:33,300
Oh, I hate to admit it, but you're--

344
00:15:34,560 --> 00:15:35,580
You're probably right.

345
00:15:37,200 --> 00:15:38,560
How'd you get to be so smart?

346
00:15:40,180 --> 00:15:40,920
I read a lot.

347
00:15:43,080 --> 00:15:44,680
Just when I thought we could be friends.

348
00:15:49,180 --> 00:15:52,060
Oh, hey, Rach. I just heard. I'm so sorry.

349
00:15:52,400 --> 00:15:53,800
Oh, thank you....

350
00:15:53,900 --> 00:15:56,900
You still don't know my name, do you?

351
00:15:58,380 --> 00:15:59,920
Well, now I don't have to.

352
00:16:04,420 --> 00:16:07,420
Ross, what is taking you so long?

353
00:16:14,620 --> 00:16:17,000
I'm sorry. It's almost as if

354
00:16:17,000 --> 00:16:19,220
this wasn't built for a quick getaway.

355
00:16:22,580 --> 00:16:23,620
Rachel?

356
00:16:24,640 --> 00:16:27,260
Mark? Oh, my God.

357
00:16:27,300 --> 00:16:28,060
How have you been?

358
00:16:28,760 --> 00:16:31,220
Fantastic. You remember Ross.

359
00:16:31,514 --> 00:16:33,244
Sure.

360
00:16:33,620 --> 00:16:34,240
What's with the chair?

361
00:16:37,120 --> 00:16:38,220
You know, you can't always

362
00:16:38,300 --> 00:16:40,380
get a seat on the subway, so....

363
00:16:42,680 --> 00:16:43,120
Clever.

364
00:16:44,540 --> 00:16:45,580
So how are you?

365
00:16:46,140 --> 00:16:48,240
You're not catching me on my best day.

366
00:16:48,700 --> 00:16:51,840
Yeah, a box full of your desk stuff doesn't say "big promotion."

367
00:16:51,940 --> 00:16:53,060
No, but it's good.

368
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:55,000
You know, I'm gonna take some time off...

369
00:16:55,000 --> 00:16:57,260
- ...and do charity work. - Are you sure?

370
00:16:57,860 --> 00:16:59,220
We may have something at Louis Vuitton.

371
00:16:59,800 --> 00:17:01,040
Screw charity work. What do you got?

372
00:17:02,540 --> 00:17:03,940
Why don't we have dinner and talk?

373
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:07,020
- Great. I'll call you. - Okay.

374
00:17:07,700 --> 00:17:08,260
Nice to see you again.

375
00:17:08,280 --> 00:17:09,700
Yeah. Yeah. I got tenure.

376
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:17,760
Oh, my God.

377
00:17:17,840 --> 00:17:20,480
See? I told you something good would come along.

378
00:17:20,900 --> 00:17:22,200
And he seemed really nice.

379
00:17:22,300 --> 00:17:23,700
I've met him before?

380
00:17:24,000 --> 00:17:25,700
Ross, that's Mark.

381
00:17:25,700 --> 00:17:27,420
From Bloomingdale's?

382
00:17:27,420 --> 00:17:29,740
You were insanely jealous of him.

383
00:17:30,020 --> 00:17:31,700
- That is Mark? - Yes.

384
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:33,120
I hate that guy.

385
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:35,800
No, no, no.

386
00:17:35,900 --> 00:17:37,400
You cannot go to dinner with him.

387
00:17:37,400 --> 00:17:39,180
What? You don't want me to get a job?

388
00:17:39,520 --> 00:17:40,680
Yeah, I'm sure he'll give you a job.

389
00:17:40,700 --> 00:17:42,780
Maybe make you his "sex-cretary."

390
00:17:44,420 --> 00:17:46,960
I'm serious. I just don't trust that guy, okay?

391
00:17:47,360 --> 00:17:48,040
Ross. You know what--?

392
00:17:48,420 --> 00:17:49,980
Okay, let's talk about it later. There comes security.

393
00:18:02,180 --> 00:18:03,460
Oh, I love this street.

394
00:18:04,040 --> 00:18:08,400
The trees and the big front yards and the actual picket fences.

395
00:18:08,600 --> 00:18:11,320
Man, those two dogs are going at it.

396
00:18:14,340 --> 00:18:16,560
Hey. Where you been?

397
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,700
Oh, just, you know, looking around.

398
00:18:19,000 --> 00:18:19,680
But you know what?

399
00:18:20,780 --> 00:18:22,360
This house is great.

400
00:18:23,040 --> 00:18:24,400
Really? What changed your mind?

401
00:18:25,240 --> 00:18:28,160
The little girl who lives here made me feel better about the whole thing.

402
00:18:29,180 --> 00:18:31,580
Joey? There was a little girl who lived here,

403
00:18:31,580 --> 00:18:33,560
but she died, like, 30 years ago.

404
00:18:38,960 --> 00:18:39,400
What?

405
00:18:41,380 --> 00:18:42,700
I'm just messing with you.

406
00:18:44,620 --> 00:18:45,460
That's not funny.

407
00:18:45,760 --> 00:18:47,480
You know I'm afraid of little-girl ghosts.

408
00:18:49,720 --> 00:18:50,760
Now that you're okay with the house,

409
00:18:50,760 --> 00:18:51,900
do you want to go see your room?

410
00:18:52,694 --> 00:18:53,574
What?

411
00:18:53,860 --> 00:18:55,240
I get my own room?

412
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,640
You don't think we'd buy a house

413
00:18:57,640 --> 00:18:59,960
and not have a Joey room, do you?

414
00:19:00,520 --> 00:19:01,700
Oh, my God.

415
00:19:05,240 --> 00:19:06,740
Hey, can I have an aquarium?

416
00:19:06,740 --> 00:19:07,700
And a sex swing?

417
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:11,000
No.

418
00:19:11,180 --> 00:19:13,460
Why not? I'll keep the tank clean.

419
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:18,300
After you, Ms. Bananahammock.

420
00:19:18,900 --> 00:19:20,380
Thank you, Mr. Bag.

421
00:19:22,100 --> 00:19:24,540
- Oh, hi, Rita. - How are you?

422
00:19:24,560 --> 00:19:27,056
Good. Oh, Rita's a massage client.

423
00:19:27,076 --> 00:19:27,916
Yeah.

424
00:19:28,660 --> 00:19:30,340
Why don't you introduce me?

425
00:19:33,240 --> 00:19:34,580
Rita, this is my husband.

426
00:19:36,080 --> 00:19:37,460
Why don't you tell her my name?

427
00:19:39,240 --> 00:19:43,440
Okay, I will. This is-- This is my husband, Crap Bag.

428
00:19:45,920 --> 00:19:46,860
Crap Bag?

429
00:19:47,200 --> 00:19:48,980
If you need an easy way to remember it,

430
00:19:49,160 --> 00:19:50,980
just think of a bag of crap.

431
00:19:54,180 --> 00:19:56,640
- Okay. Excuse me. - Yeah.

432
00:20:00,060 --> 00:20:01,600
Okay, fine, you made your point.

433
00:20:01,600 --> 00:20:03,720
Can you please just be Mike Hannigan again?

434
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:05,260
Only if you'll be Phoebe Buffay.

435
00:20:07,220 --> 00:20:09,680
How about--? How about Buffay-Hannigan?

436
00:20:10,240 --> 00:20:11,100
Really?

437
00:20:11,280 --> 00:20:11,800
Yeah.

438
00:20:12,010 --> 00:20:14,360
I'm Phoebe Buffay-Hannigan-Banana Hammock.

439
00:20:16,980 --> 00:20:19,380
Do you even know what a banana hammock is?

440
00:20:19,900 --> 00:20:20,960
It's a funny word.

441
00:20:21,540 --> 00:20:22,480
It's a Speedo.

442
00:20:27,660 --> 00:20:28,680
Oh, crap.

443
00:20:32,780 --> 00:20:34,940
- Hey, is Rachel here? - Nope.

444
00:20:35,980 --> 00:20:37,040
She's still at dinner?

445
00:20:37,400 --> 00:20:39,200
I guess. Why, who's she with?

446
00:20:39,320 --> 00:20:40,280
That guy, Mark...

447
00:20:40,280 --> 00:20:41,720
...from Bloomingdale's.

448
00:20:41,780 --> 00:20:43,560
She thinks he's just being nice to her.

449
00:20:43,780 --> 00:20:45,540
But I know he really wants to sleep with her.

450
00:20:45,940 --> 00:20:47,200
It's seven years ago.

451
00:20:49,880 --> 00:20:51,220
My time machine works.

452
00:20:53,760 --> 00:20:55,840
We ran into him on the street today,

453
00:20:55,840 --> 00:20:57,360
and he said he might have a job for her.

454
00:20:57,420 --> 00:20:58,980
But I know he just wants to get into her pants.

455
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:02,620
So, what if he wants to sleep with her?

456
00:21:02,620 --> 00:21:04,880
I mean, she's single, and he's cute.

457
00:21:05,120 --> 00:21:05,940
Excuse me?

458
00:21:07,520 --> 00:21:08,400
Oh, please.

459
00:21:08,960 --> 00:21:11,240
Yesterday, on the subway, you couldn't stop staring...

460
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:13,140
...at that woman with the big breasts the whole time.

461
00:21:13,440 --> 00:21:16,140
For your information, I was staring at her baby.

462
00:21:16,640 --> 00:21:17,800
We're about to be parents.

463
00:21:19,420 --> 00:21:20,300
Oh, sorry.

464
00:21:31,300 --> 00:21:33,680
- Hi, you guys. - Hi. So...

465
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:35,300
...how was dinner?

466
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:38,260
Oh, it was great. Mark is so sweet.

467
00:21:38,280 --> 00:21:40,000
Oh, yeah? Yeah, I wonder why?

468
00:21:40,100 --> 00:21:42,040
What could that smarmy letch possibly want?

469
00:21:42,040 --> 00:21:45,640
Oh, Ross. Come on. He is happily married.

470
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:47,280
His wife just had twins.

471
00:21:47,800 --> 00:21:49,160
Should we send something?

472
00:21:51,160 --> 00:21:52,680
How did the job stuff go?

473
00:21:54,120 --> 00:21:55,380
He offered me one.

474
00:21:56,600 --> 00:21:58,100
- That's great. - Congratulations.

475
00:21:58,780 --> 00:22:00,780
I know, it's amazing.

476
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:03,300
It's amazing. It's so much better

477
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:04,840
than what I had at Ralph Lauren.

478
00:22:05,120 --> 00:22:07,580
- The money is great. - Can we--?

479
00:22:07,640 --> 00:22:08,920
Can we just stop for a second?

480
00:22:08,960 --> 00:22:11,380
Who said something better would come along?

481
00:22:12,520 --> 00:22:13,380
You didn't believe me.

482
00:22:13,380 --> 00:22:15,380
I told you everything was gonna work out.

483
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:16,400
You know what?

484
00:22:16,480 --> 00:22:18,520
This calls for a bottle of lsrael's finest.

485
00:22:23,240 --> 00:22:24,780
The job is in Paris.

486
00:22:38,086 --> 00:22:41,156
I mean, this soap opera is a great gig...

487
00:22:41,160 --> 00:22:42,990
...but am I missing opportunities?

488
00:22:43,012 --> 00:22:45,872
You know, I've always thought of myself as a serious actor.

489
00:22:45,997 --> 00:22:48,577
Should I be trying to do more independent movies?

490
00:22:49,100 --> 00:22:50,420
I don't know.

491
00:22:52,340 --> 00:22:53,360
But you know what?

492
00:22:53,740 --> 00:22:54,920
I'm gonna put you on with my bear.

493
00:22:55,800 --> 00:22:56,420
Hold on.

494
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:00,240
Hey, Bailey, I need some career advice.

